WEBVTT

NOTE Synthetic transcript for evals. Company, people and figures are invented.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:15.000
<v Aida Bekova>Good morning everyone. Today is Thursday, October 22nd. The goal of this session is to agree the scope of the returns portal for the first release.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:31.000
<v Tom Reyes>Thanks Aida. From the operations side, the big pain is that returns come in by email and phone today, and my team re-types every one of them into the warehouse system.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:48.000
<v Priya Nair>And on the IT side the warehouse system is the old WMS. It has an API, but it's not well documented.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:25.000
<v Aida Bekova>Let's start with who the portal is for. Business customers, consumers, or both in the first release?

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:52.000
<v Tom Reyes>B2B returns go through account managers and have contract rules. That's a different beast. I'd keep the first release to consumers only.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:02:05.000
<v Lena Novak>Agreed from finance. B2B credit notes are a separate process anyway.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:14.000
<v Priya Nair>Fine with me.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:24.000
<v Aida Bekova>So we agree: release one covers consumer returns only, B2B is out of scope for release one.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.000
<v Tom Reyes>Yes.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:05:02.000
<v Aida Bekova>Next, refunds. How should the customer get their money back?

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:30.000
<v Lena Novak>Always to the original payment method. No store credit, no bank transfers to a different account. That's a fraud rule for us.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:40.000
<v Tom Reyes>Customers sometimes ask for store credit, but okay, original payment method only.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:48.000
<v Aida Bekova>Decision then: refunds go only to the original payment method.

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:51.000
<v Lena Novak>Correct.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:40.000
<v Tom Reyes>One idea: we could print a QR code on the return label, so the warehouse scans it and the return is matched automatically.

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:58.000
<v Priya Nair>I like it, but I need to check whether the WMS can read QR codes at all. Let's not decide that today.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:52.000
<v Lena Novak>What about large refunds? Today anything above 500 euros needs a manager's approval. Who approves that in the portal?

00:09:53.000 --> 00:10:10.000
<v Tom Reyes>Good question. I don't know if that's my team or finance. We need to clarify it.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:40.000
<v Aida Bekova>Let's agree next steps. Priya, can you send us the WMS API documentation?

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:50.000
<v Priya Nair>Yes, I'll send it by Friday the 30th.

00:11:51.000 --> 00:12:10.000
<v Aida Bekova>Tom, could you confirm the list of return reasons your team uses?

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:22.000
<v Tom Reyes>Sure, I'll send it before next Tuesday's session.

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:45.000
<v Lena Novak>And someone should check whether we charge a return fee for consumers. I'm not sure the policy is still current.

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:52.000
<v Aida Bekova>Noted. Let's figure out who owns that.

00:12:53.000 --> 00:13:05.000
<v Aida Bekova>Thank you all. I'll send the summary today.
